BOOK.add({
  subject: "eng",
  id: "eng-03",
  title: "Use of important Conjunctions — संयोजक",
  notes: "\n    <h3>Conjunction (संयोजक) क्या है?</h3>\n    <p>वह शब्द जो दो शब्दों, वाक्यांशों या उपवाक्यों (clauses) को जोड़ता है — <b>Conjunction</b> कहलाता है। जैसे: Ram <b>and</b> Shyam are friends. (राम और श्याम मित्र हैं।) I was ill, <b>so</b> I did not go. (मैं बीमार था, इसलिए नहीं गया।)<br>\n    परीक्षा में मुख्यतः तीन बातें पूछी जाती हैं — (1) <b>सही जोड़ी</b> (no sooner … <b>than</b>, hardly … <b>when</b>), (2) <b>Correlative का सही स्थान</b> (parallelism), (3) <b>Verb का सामंजस्य</b> (either…or, neither…nor के साथ)।</p>\n\n    <h3>1. Coordinating Conjunctions (समानाधिकरण संयोजक)</h3>\n    <p>ये समान स्तर के दो भागों (दो स्वतंत्र वाक्यों / दो शब्दों) को जोड़ते हैं। याद रखें <b>FANBOYS</b>: <b>F</b>or, <b>A</b>nd, <b>N</b>or, <b>B</b>ut, <b>O</b>r, <b>Y</b>et, <b>S</b>o।</p>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>Conjunction</th><th>भाव (प्रकार)</th><th>उदाहरण व हिन्दी अर्थ</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>and, as well as, both…and, not only…but also</b></td><td>Cumulative (जोड़ना)</td><td>He is poor <b>and</b> honest. — वह ग़रीब और ईमानदार है।</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>but, yet, still, while, whereas, however, nevertheless</b></td><td>Adversative (विरोध)</td><td>He is poor <b>but</b> honest. — वह ग़रीब है पर ईमानदार है।</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>or, either…or, neither…nor, else, otherwise</b></td><td>Alternative (विकल्प)</td><td>Work hard, <b>or</b> you will fail. — मेहनत करो, वरना फ़ेल हो जाओगे।</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>so, therefore, hence, for, consequently</b></td><td>Illative (परिणाम/कारण)</td><td>He was tired, <b>so</b> he slept. — वह थका था, इसलिए सो गया।</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <p><b>'For'</b> (क्योंकि) coordinating conjunction है और वाक्य के आरंभ में नहीं आता: <i>He must be ill, <b>for</b> he looks pale.</i> (वह बीमार होगा, क्योंकि पीला दिख रहा है।)</p>\n\n    <h3>2. Subordinating Conjunctions (अधीन संयोजक)</h3>\n    <p>ये एक <b>आश्रित उपवाक्य (dependent clause)</b> को मुख्य उपवाक्य से जोड़ते हैं।</p>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>भाव</th><th>Conjunctions</th><th>उदाहरण</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>समय (Time)</td><td>when, while, as, before, after, since, till, until, as soon as, whenever</td><td>Wait <b>till</b> I come. <b>As soon as</b> he saw me, he ran away.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>कारण (Cause)</td><td>because, since, as, for, now that</td><td>I stayed at home <b>because</b> it was raining.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>उद्देश्य (Purpose)</td><td>that, so that, in order that, lest</td><td>He works hard <b>so that</b> he may succeed.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>परिणाम (Result)</td><td>so…that, such…that</td><td>He is <b>so</b> weak <b>that</b> he cannot walk.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>शर्त (Condition)</td><td>if, unless, provided (that), in case, on condition that, supposing</td><td><b>Unless</b> you work hard, you will fail.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>विरोध/रियायत (Concession)</td><td>though, although, even if, even though, however</td><td><b>Though</b> he is poor, he is honest.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>तुलना (Comparison)</td><td>than, as…as, so…as</td><td>He is taller <b>than</b> I. She is <b>as</b> tall <b>as</b> her mother.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>रीति (Manner)</td><td>as, as if, as though</td><td>Do <b>as</b> I tell you. He talks <b>as if</b> he were a king.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>स्थान (Place)</td><td>where, wherever</td><td>Go <b>wherever</b> you like.</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <h3>3. Correlative Conjunctions (सहसंबंधी — जोड़ी वाले)</h3>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>जोड़ी</th><th>अर्थ</th><th>उदाहरण</th><th>ध्यान दें</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>either … or</b></td><td>या तो … या</td><td><b>Either</b> you <b>or</b> he has to go.</td><td>Verb निकटतम subject के अनुसार</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>neither … nor</b></td><td>न तो … न ही</td><td><b>Neither</b> Ram <b>nor</b> his friends were there.</td><td>neither के साथ 'or' गलत; दोहरा नकार (not…neither) गलत</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>both … and</b></td><td>दोनों … और</td><td><b>Both</b> Sita <b>and</b> Gita are clever.</td><td>both के साथ 'as well as' गलत; verb plural</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>not only … but also</b></td><td>न केवल … बल्कि … भी</td><td>He is <b>not only</b> intelligent <b>but also</b> hardworking.</td><td>Verb दूसरे subject के अनुसार; वाक्य आरंभ में हो तो inversion</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>whether … or</b></td><td>चाहे … या</td><td>I don't know <b>whether</b> he will come <b>or</b> not.</td><td>whether के साथ 'or' (than/nor नहीं)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>though / although … yet</b></td><td>यद्यपि … तथापि</td><td><b>Though</b> he is poor, <b>yet</b> he is honest.</td><td>though के साथ 'but' नहीं</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>no sooner … than</b></td><td>ज्यों ही … त्यों ही</td><td><b>No sooner</b> had he reached <b>than</b> it began to rain.</td><td>'than' ही — 'when/then' नहीं; inversion (had he)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>hardly / scarcely / barely … when (before)</b></td><td>मुश्किल से … कि</td><td><b>Hardly</b> had I left <b>when</b> the bus came.</td><td>'when' या 'before' — 'than' नहीं</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>so … that</b></td><td>इतना … कि</td><td>He is <b>so</b> tired <b>that</b> he cannot walk.</td><td>so के साथ 'that'; 'too…to' का समानार्थी</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>such … that / such … as</b></td><td>ऐसा … कि / ऐसा … जैसा</td><td>It was <b>such</b> a hot day <b>that</b> we stayed in. He is not <b>such</b> a fool <b>as</b> he looks.</td><td>such … as (relative)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>as … as</b> / <b>so … as</b></td><td>उतना … जितना</td><td>He is <b>as</b> tall <b>as</b> his father. He is not <b>so</b> tall <b>as</b> his father.</td><td>so…as प्रायः नकारात्मक वाक्य में</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>rather … than / would rather … than</b></td><td>के बजाय</td><td>I would <b>rather</b> die <b>than</b> beg.</td><td>rather के साथ 'than'; दोनों ओर V1</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>lest … should</b></td><td>कहीं ऐसा न हो कि</td><td>Walk carefully <b>lest</b> you <b>should</b> fall.</td><td>lest के साथ केवल 'should' (या V1); 'not' कभी नहीं</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>the same … as / that</b></td><td>वही … जो</td><td>This is <b>the same</b> pen <b>as</b> I lost / <b>that</b> I lost.</td><td>—</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>scarcely … when</b></td><td>मुश्किल से … कि</td><td><b>Scarcely</b> had he gone <b>when</b> she came.</td><td>—</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>other … than / else … but (than)</b></td><td>के अलावा</td><td>He has no <b>other</b> option <b>than</b> to resign.</td><td>other के साथ 'than' (but/except भी चलता है)</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <h3>4. Correlatives में Parallelism (सम-संरचना)</h3>\n    <p>जोड़ी के दोनों भागों के बाद <b>एक ही प्रकार का शब्द</b> आना चाहिए (noun-noun, verb-verb, adjective-adjective)।</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li>गलत: He <b>not only</b> lost his money <b>but also</b> his reputation. → सही: He lost <b>not only</b> his money <b>but also</b> his reputation. (दोनों के बाद noun)</li>\n      <li>गलत: She <b>either</b> came on Monday <b>or</b> Tuesday. → सही: She came <b>either</b> on Monday <b>or</b> on Tuesday.</li>\n      <li>गलत: He is <b>both</b> clever <b>and</b> a hard worker. → सही: He is <b>both</b> clever <b>and</b> hardworking.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>5. Inversion (उलटा क्रम) — नकारात्मक/सीमित शब्द आरंभ में</h3>\n    <p>जब <b>No sooner, Hardly, Scarcely, Not only, Never, Seldom, Rarely, Neither, Nor, Not until, Only then</b> से वाक्य शुरू हो तो <b>सहायक क्रिया (auxiliary) subject से पहले</b> आती है (प्रश्नवाचक जैसा क्रम):</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li><b>No sooner did</b> he see the police <b>than</b> he ran away. (No sooner he saw… गलत)</li>\n      <li><b>Hardly had</b> we reached the station <b>when</b> the train left.</li>\n      <li><b>Not only did</b> he abuse me, <b>but</b> he <b>also</b> beat me.</li>\n      <li>He does not like tea, <b>nor does</b> he like coffee.</li>\n      <li><b>Not until</b> he came <b>did</b> I leave.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>6. Verb Agreement — जुड़े हुए Subjects</h3>\n    <table>\n      <tr><th>संरचना</th><th>Verb किसके अनुसार</th><th>उदाहरण</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>A <b>and</b> B / <b>Both</b> A <b>and</b> B</td><td>सदा plural (एक व्यक्ति/विचार हो तो singular)</td><td>Ram and Shyam <b>are</b> brothers.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>Either</b> A <b>or</b> B / <b>Neither</b> A <b>nor</b> B / A <b>or</b> B</td><td>B (निकटतम) के अनुसार</td><td>Neither the minister nor his secretaries <b>were</b> present.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>Not only</b> A <b>but also</b> B</td><td>B के अनुसार</td><td>Not only the students but also the teacher <b>was</b> late.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>A <b>as well as / with / along with / together with / besides / and not / rather than</b> B</td><td>A (पहले) के अनुसार</td><td>The captain, as well as the players, <b>has</b> arrived.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><b>Not</b> A <b>but</b> B</td><td>B के अनुसार</td><td>Not the players but the captain <b>was</b> blamed.</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"tip\">Person का क्रम-भेद: plural subject को plural verb के पास रखना शैली की दृष्टि से अच्छा है — \"Neither he nor I <b>am</b> wrong\" व्याकरण से सही है पर \"Neither of us is wrong\" अधिक सहज है।</div>\n\n    <h3>7. महत्वपूर्ण Conjunctions — विस्तार से</h3>\n    <h4>(क) Unless / Until / Till</h4>\n    <p><b>Unless</b> = if not (शर्त) — इसलिए unless के साथ 'not' नहीं आता: <i>Unless you work hard, you will fail.</i> (Unless you do not work… गलत)।<br>\n    <b>Until / Till</b> = जब तक नहीं (समय) — इनमें भी 'not' नहीं: <i>Wait here until I return.</i> (until I do not return गलत)।<br>\n    Unless व until दोनों के बाद भविष्य के लिए Simple Present आता है (will नहीं)।</p>\n    <h4>(ख) Because / Since / As / For</h4>\n    <p><b>Because</b> — प्रबल, सीधा कारण, प्रायः नई सूचना: <i>He failed because he was lazy.</i><br>\n    <b>Since / As</b> — ज्ञात या कमज़ोर कारण, प्रायः वाक्य के आरंभ में: <i>As it was late, we went home. Since you are tired, rest a while.</i><br>\n    <b>For</b> — अतिरिक्त कारण/प्रमाण, comma के बाद, वाक्य के मध्य में।<br>\n    <b>The reason … is that</b> (because नहीं): <i>The reason why he failed <b>is that</b> he was lazy.</i> (\"The reason is because\" गलत)।<br>\n    <b>Because</b> के साथ 'so' / 'therefore' नहीं: \"Because he was ill, so he did not come\" गलत।</p>\n    <h4>(ग) Though / Although</h4>\n    <p>दोनों का अर्थ 'यद्यपि'। साथ में <b>yet</b> या comma आता है, <b>but नहीं</b>: <i>Although he worked hard, (yet) he failed.</i> 'Though' वाक्य के अंत में adverb के रूप में भी आता है ('तथापि'): <i>He failed, though.</i> 'Although' अंत में नहीं आता। <b>Even though</b> = 'हालाँकि' (ज़ोरदार)।</p>\n    <h4>(घ) Lest</h4>\n    <p>Lest = <b>कहीं ऐसा न हो कि</b> (that … not)। इसमें नकारात्मक भाव पहले से है, इसलिए <b>lest के साथ 'not' नहीं</b> और सहायक क्रिया <b>'should'</b> ही आती है (would/will/may नहीं): <i>Work hard lest you should fail.</i> (मेहनत करो, कहीं फ़ेल न हो जाओ।)</p>\n    <h4>(ङ) As well as</h4>\n    <p>As well as = 'के साथ-साथ' (भी)। Verb पहले subject के अनुसार। 'Both' के साथ 'as well as' कभी नहीं: \"Both Ram as well as Shyam\" गलत → Both Ram <b>and</b> Shyam।</p>\n    <h4>(च) So that / In order that</h4>\n    <p>उद्देश्य बताते हैं; इनके बाद <b>may/might/can/could</b> आता है: <i>He ran fast so that he might catch the bus.</i> (should नहीं; should 'lest' के साथ)।</p>\n    <h4>(छ) That / If / Whether</h4>\n    <p>संदेह, प्रश्न के अप्रत्यक्ष कथन में <b>if/whether</b>: <i>He asked me <b>whether</b> I would come.</i> Doubt के बाद: <i>I doubt <b>whether</b> he will come</i> (सकारात्मक), पर नकारात्मक में <i>I do not doubt <b>that</b> he will come.</i></p>\n    <h4>(ज) Till / Since के समय-संकेत</h4>\n    <p><b>Since</b> (कारण अर्थ में 'चूँकि', समय अर्थ में 'से') — \"It is two years since he left\" (since के बाद Past Simple)। \"Since\" से पहले वाले मुख्य वाक्य में Present Perfect: <i>I have known him since he was a child.</i></p>\n    <h4>(झ) While / Whereas</h4>\n    <p><b>While</b> = जब (समय, continuous कार्य) या जबकि (विरोध): <i>While I was reading, the light went off.</i> <b>Whereas</b> = जबकि (तुलना/विरोध): <i>He is rich, whereas his brother is poor.</i></p>\n    <h4>(ञ) Or / Nor</h4>\n    <p>नकारात्मक वाक्य के बाद दूसरा नकारात्मक भाग जोड़ने हेतु <b>nor</b> (inversion के साथ): <i>I cannot sing, nor can I dance.</i> पर 'not … or' भी सही: <i>He did not eat or drink.</i> 'Neither' के साथ सदा 'nor'।</p>\n    <h4>(ट) Too…to / So…that रूपांतरण</h4>\n    <p><i>He is <b>too</b> weak <b>to</b> walk.</i> = <i>He is <b>so</b> weak <b>that</b> he <b>cannot</b> walk.</i> — 'too…to' में 'not' नहीं लगता क्योंकि 'too' में ही नकार है।</p>\n    <h4>(ठ) Conjunction की पुनरावृत्ति से बचें</h4>\n    <p>\"Although … but\", \"Because … so\", \"Since … therefore\", \"Unless … not\", \"Lest … not\", \"Until … not\", \"Both … as well as\", \"Hardly … than\", \"No sooner … when\" — ये सभी परीक्षा में बार-बार पूछी जाने वाली गलत जोड़ियाँ हैं।</p>\n  ",
  extra: "\n    <h3>गहन तथ्य — जो सामान्य पाठक नहीं जानता</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li><b>No sooner — Comparative का रूप:</b> 'sooner' comparative है, इसलिए इसके साथ 'than' आता है; 'hardly/scarcely' comparative नहीं, इसलिए 'when/before'। यही तर्क याद रखने की सबसे पक्की ट्रिक है।</li>\n      <li><b>Tense का मेल:</b> No sooner/Hardly वाले वाक्य में पहले भाग में Past Perfect (had + V3) या did + V1 और दूसरे भाग में Simple Past: \"No sooner <b>had</b> the bell <b>rung</b> than the students <b>rushed</b> out.\" \"No sooner <b>did</b> the bell <b>ring</b> than…\" भी सही।</li>\n      <li><b>Hardly — 'मुश्किल से' बनाम 'कठिनाई से':</b> hardly ≠ hard। \"He works hard\" (कड़ी मेहनत) बनाम \"He hardly works\" (बहुत कम काम करता है)। hardly स्वयं नकारात्मक है, इसलिए \"hardly … not\" या \"can't hardly\" गलत।</li>\n      <li><b>Seldom or never / seldom if ever:</b> सही मुहावरे हैं; \"seldom or ever\" गलत।</li>\n      <li><b>Scarcely … when बनाम Scarcely … than:</b> 'than' कभी नहीं — \"Scarcely had he finished when…\"।</li>\n      <li><b>Not only … but also में 'also' का लोप:</b> \"Not only he but his wife too came\" भी स्वीकार्य; परंतु 'but' अनिवार्य है।</li>\n      <li><b>Since का दोहरा अर्थ:</b> \"Since he was ill, he stayed at home\" (कारण — चूँकि) बनाम \"I have not seen him since he left\" (समय — जब से)। परीक्षा में अर्थ पहचानना पूछा जाता है।</li>\n      <li><b>As का पाँच अर्थ:</b> समय (As he entered, the lights went off), कारण (As he was ill, he left), रीति (Do as I say), तुलना (as tall as), विरोध (Poor as he is, he is honest = यद्यपि वह ग़रीब है)।</li>\n      <li><b>'Poor as he is' संरचना:</b> Adjective + as + subject + verb = though — \"Young as she is, she is very wise.\" यहाँ 'as' का अर्थ 'though' है — परीक्षा में rearrangement में आता है।</li>\n      <li><b>Like बनाम As:</b> like preposition है (noun/pronoun लेता है) — \"He runs like a deer\"; as conjunction है (clause लेता है) — \"Do as I do\"। \"Do like I do\" औपचारिक अंग्रेज़ी में गलत।</li>\n      <li><b>Lest के बाद V1 (subjunctive):</b> अमेरिकी अंग्रेज़ी में \"lest he fall\" भी सही; पर परीक्षा का उत्तर सामान्यतः \"lest he should fall\"।</li>\n      <li><b>Until व unless में अंतर:</b> \"I will not go until you come\" (समय — जब तक तुम न आओ) बनाम \"I will not go unless you come\" (शर्त — यदि तुम न आओ तो)। मुख्य वाक्य में 'not' हो सकता है, आश्रित वाक्य में नहीं।</li>\n      <li><b>Whether के बाद 'or not':</b> \"Whether or not he comes\" और \"whether he comes or not\" दोनों सही; पर \"if or not\" गलत।</li>\n      <li><b>Doubt का नियम:</b> सकारात्मक वाक्य में doubt + whether/if; नकारात्मक/प्रश्नवाचक में doubt + that — \"There is no doubt that he is honest.\"</li>\n      <li><b>Scarcely any / Hardly any:</b> \"There is scarcely any water\" — any के साथ, no के साथ नहीं।</li>\n      <li><b>Such as बनाम Such that:</b> such as = जैसे कि (उदाहरण) — \"Fruits such as mango and banana\"; such that = इस प्रकार कि (परिणाम)।</li>\n      <li><b>Directly / Immediately / The moment:</b> ये भी 'as soon as' की तरह conjunction के रूप में प्रयुक्त होते हैं — \"The moment he arrived, the meeting began.\"</li>\n      <li><b>Neither … nor के साथ pronoun:</b> \"Neither Ram nor Shyam has done <b>his</b> work\" — singular subjects हों तो pronoun singular।</li>\n    </ul>\n  ",
  questions: [
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: No sooner had he reached the station ______ the train left.","o":["than","when","then","before"],"a":0,"e":"'No sooner' के साथ सदा 'than' आता है (sooner comparative है)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Hardly had I gone out ______ it started raining.","o":["than","when","then","but"],"a":1,"e":"'Hardly/Scarcely' के साथ 'when' (या before) आता है, 'than' नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Scarcely had the teacher entered ______ the students stood up.","o":["than","then","when","that"],"a":2,"e":"'Scarcely … when' सही जोड़ी है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Neither Ram ______ Shyam came to the party.","o":["or","and","but","nor"],"a":3,"e":"'Neither' के साथ सदा 'nor' आता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Either you ______ your brother must go.","o":["or","nor","and","but"],"a":0,"e":"'Either' के साथ 'or' आता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is not only clever ______ hardworking.","o":["and also","but also","as well as","so also"],"a":1,"e":"'Not only' की जोड़ी 'but also' है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Both Sita ______ Gita are good singers.","o":["as well as","or","and","with"],"a":2,"e":"'Both' के साथ केवल 'and' आता है; 'both … as well as' गलत।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Walk carefully lest you ______ fall.","o":["would","may","will","should"],"a":3,"e":"'Lest' के साथ 'should' आता है — lest you should fall।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ he is poor, he is honest.","o":["Though","But","Because","Unless"],"a":0,"e":"विरोध (यद्यपि) का भाव — Though he is poor, he is honest।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Though he worked hard, ______ he failed.","o":["but","yet","so","and"],"a":1,"e":"'Though/Although' के साथ 'yet' (या केवल comma) आता है, 'but' नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ you work hard, you will not pass.","o":["If","Until","Unless","Since"],"a":2,"e":"'Unless' = if not — Unless you work hard (यदि मेहनत नहीं करोगे)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Wait here ______ I come back.","o":["unless","lest","since","until"],"a":3,"e":"समय-सीमा (जब तक) के लिए 'until/till'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I don't know ______ he will come or not.","o":["whether","that","unless","neither"],"a":0,"e":"'Or not' के साथ 'whether' की जोड़ी — whether … or not।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is so weak ______ he cannot walk.","o":["than","that","as","so"],"a":1,"e":"'So … that' — इतना … कि।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I would rather die ______ beg.","o":["that","then","than","but"],"a":2,"e":"'Rather … than' — भीख माँगने के बजाय मरना पसंद करूँगा।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is as tall ______ his father.","o":["than","so","like","as"],"a":3,"e":"समानता की तुलना 'as … as' — as tall as।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He ran fast ______ he might catch the bus.","o":["so that","lest","unless","such that"],"a":0,"e":"उद्देश्य के लिए 'so that' + may/might।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He must be ill, ______ he looks pale.","o":["so","for","but","or"],"a":1,"e":"'For' (क्योंकि) — अतिरिक्त कारण/प्रमाण बताने वाला coordinating conjunction।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He was tired, ______ he went to bed early.","o":["for","but","so","yet"],"a":2,"e":"परिणाम बताने हेतु 'so' (इसलिए)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Work hard, ______ you will fail.","o":["and","but","so","or"],"a":3,"e":"'Or' = वरना/अन्यथा — Work hard, or you will fail।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Make hay ______ the sun shines.","o":["while","until","unless","lest"],"a":0,"e":"'While' = जब तक/जब — मुहावरा: Make hay while the sun shines।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: It was ______ a hot day that we stayed indoors.","o":["so","such","very","too"],"a":1,"e":"'Such + a + adjective + noun + that' — such a hot day that।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is not such a fool ______ he looks.","o":["that","than","as","so"],"a":2,"e":"'Such … as' — not such a fool as he looks।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is rich, ______ his brother is poor.","o":["because","unless","lest","whereas"],"a":3,"e":"दो विपरीत तथ्यों की तुलना में 'whereas' (जबकि)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ he saw the police, he ran away.","o":["As soon as","Unless","Lest","Though"],"a":0,"e":"'As soon as' — ज्यों ही उसने पुलिस देखी।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: The reason why he failed is ______ he did not study.","o":["because","that","why","as"],"a":1,"e":"'The reason … is that' सही संरचना है; 'reason … because' दोहराव है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I cannot sing, ______ can I dance.","o":["or","and","nor","but"],"a":2,"e":"नकारात्मक वाक्य के बाद दूसरा नकारात्मक भाग 'nor' + inversion (can I) से।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: This is the same book ______ I lost last week.","o":["which","what","who","that"],"a":3,"e":"'The same … that/as' — this is the same book that I lost।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Do ______ I tell you.","o":["as","like","so","than"],"a":0,"e":"Clause (I tell you) से पहले conjunction 'as'; 'like' preposition है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He talks ______ he were a king.","o":["like","as if","so that","as well as"],"a":1,"e":"काल्पनिक तुलना में 'as if' + were।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I have known him ______ he was a child.","o":["for","from","since","when"],"a":2,"e":"समय-बिंदु से आरंभ — 'since he was a child'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ it was raining, we did not go out.","o":["Unless","Although","Lest","As"],"a":3,"e":"कारण (चूँकि) — As it was raining।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Take an umbrella ______ it rains.","o":["in case","unless","until","lest not"],"a":0,"e":"'In case' = यदि ऐसा हो जाए (एहतियात) — take an umbrella in case it rains।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: You can borrow my book ______ you return it tomorrow.","o":["unless","provided","lest","though"],"a":1,"e":"'Provided (that)' = इस शर्त पर कि।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is ______ weak to walk.","o":["so","very","too","such"],"a":2,"e":"'Too … to' = इतना … कि नहीं — too weak to walk।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Young ______ she is, she is very wise.","o":["though","if","since","as"],"a":3,"e":"'Adjective + as + subject + verb' = though — Young as she is (यद्यपि वह युवा है)।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: No sooner did he reach home (A) / when (B) / it began to rain. (C) / No error (D)","o":["No sooner did he reach home","when","it began to rain","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'No sooner' के साथ 'than' आता है, 'when' नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Hardly had she (A) / finished her work (B) / than the guests arrived. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Hardly had she","finished her work","than the guests arrived","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'Hardly' के साथ 'when' — when the guests arrived।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Although he is rich (A) / but he is (B) / very miserly. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Although he is rich","but he is","very miserly","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Although' के साथ 'but' नहीं आता; 'yet' या केवल comma।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Unless you do not (A) / work hard, (B) / you will not succeed. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Unless you do not","work hard,","you will not succeed.","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'Unless' में नकार पहले से है — 'Unless you work hard'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Run fast (A) / lest you should not (B) / miss the train. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Run fast","lest you should not","miss the train","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Lest' में नकारात्मक भाव निहित है — lest you should miss।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Both Ram (A) / as well as Shyam (B) / are absent today. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Both Ram","as well as Shyam","are absent today","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Both' की जोड़ी 'and' है — Both Ram and Shyam।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Neither he (A) / or his friends (B) / were present. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Neither he","or his friends","were present","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Neither' के साथ 'nor' — nor his friends।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Because he was ill, (A) / so he (B) / did not attend the class. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Because he was ill,","so he","did not attend the class.","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Because' और 'so' एक साथ नहीं आते — 'so' हटाइए।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Wait here (A) / until I do not (B) / return. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Wait here","until I do not","return","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Until' में 'not' नहीं लगता — until I return।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He not only lost (A) / his money but also (B) / his reputation. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He not only lost","his money but also","his reputation","No error"],"a":0,"e":"Parallelism: 'not only' को 'his money' से ठीक पहले रखें — He lost not only his money but also his reputation।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Scarcely had (A) / he left (B) / than she came. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Scarcely had","he left","than she came","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'Scarcely' के साथ 'when' — when she came।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Not only he abused me (A) / but also (B) / beat me. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Not only he abused me","but also","beat me","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'Not only' वाक्य के आरंभ में हो तो inversion — Not only did he abuse me, but he also beat me।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: The reason (A) / for his absence is (B) / because he was ill. (C) / No error (D)","o":["The reason","for his absence is","because he was ill","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'The reason … is that' — that he was ill।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Neither the teacher (A) / nor the students (B) / was present in the class. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Neither the teacher","nor the students","was present in the class","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'Neither … nor' में verb निकटतम subject (students, plural) के अनुसार — were present।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: The captain, (A) / as well as the players, (B) / were injured. (C) / No error (D)","o":["The captain,","as well as the players,","were injured","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'As well as' में verb पहले subject (captain) के अनुसार — was injured।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Not only the students (A) / but also the teacher (B) / were late. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Not only the students","but also the teacher","were late","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'Not only … but also' में verb दूसरे subject (teacher) के अनुसार — was late।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He is (A) / both clever (B) / and a hard worker. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He is","both clever","and a hard worker","No error"],"a":2,"e":"Parallelism: clever (adjective) के साथ adjective — and hardworking।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: She came either (A) / on Monday (B) / or Tuesday. (C) / No error (D)","o":["She came either","on Monday","or Tuesday","No error"],"a":2,"e":"Parallelism: 'either on Monday' के साथ 'or on Tuesday' होना चाहिए।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: No sooner he had (A) / heard the news (B) / than he fainted. (C) / No error (D)","o":["No sooner he had","heard the news","than he fainted","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'No sooner' से आरंभ होने पर inversion — No sooner had he heard…।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: I doubt (A) / that he (B) / will pass. (C) / No error (D)","o":["I doubt","that he","will pass","No error"],"a":1,"e":"सकारात्मक वाक्य में doubt के बाद 'whether/if' — I doubt whether he will pass।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He is (A) / so tired that (B) / he can walk no farther. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He is","so tired that","he can walk no farther","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'So … that' सही जोड़ी है और 'no farther' (और दूर नहीं) भी सही — कोई त्रुटि नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He is too weak (A) / that he (B) / cannot walk. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He is too weak","that he","cannot walk","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'Too' के साथ 'to' आता है — He is too weak to walk; या 'so weak that he cannot walk'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Seldom or ever (A) / does he (B) / come late. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Seldom or ever","does he","come late","No error"],"a":0,"e":"सही मुहावरा 'seldom or never' / 'seldom if ever' है।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Since he was (A) / a child he (B) / is living here. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Since he was","a child he","is living here","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'Since' के साथ मुख्य वाक्य में Present Perfect Continuous — has been living here।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: I will wait (A) / till you will (B) / finish your work. (C) / No error (D)","o":["I will wait","till you will","finish your work","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Till' वाले time clause में future के लिए Simple Present — till you finish।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Hardly had I (A) / reached the station (B) / when the train left. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Hardly had I","reached the station","when the train left","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'Hardly … when' सही जोड़ी व inversion (had I) सही — कोई त्रुटि नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Either he (A) / or I (B) / are going to Raipur. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Either he","or I","are going to Raipur","No error"],"a":2,"e":"Verb निकटतम subject 'I' के अनुसार — am going।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He did not come (A) / since he was (B) / ill. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He did not come","since he was","ill","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'Since' = चूँकि (कारण) — वाक्य शुद्ध है।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["No sooner had the bell rung than the students rushed out.","No sooner had the bell rung when the students rushed out.","No sooner the bell had rung than the students rushed out.","No sooner did the bell rang than the students rushed out."],"a":0,"e":"'No sooner had + subject + V3 … than' — inversion व 'than' दोनों सही; did के बाद V1 (ring) आता।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Hardly he had sat down than the phone rang.","Hardly had he sat down than the phone rang.","Hardly he sat down when the phone rang.","Hardly had he sat down when the phone rang."],"a":3,"e":"'Hardly had + subject + V3 … when' — inversion और 'when' दोनों आवश्यक।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you do not hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you will hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you hurry, you will not miss the bus."],"a":0,"e":"Unless = if not; उसके साथ not नहीं और future के लिए Simple Present।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Neither of them nor I am going.","Neither he nor I are going.","Neither he nor I am going.","Neither he or I am going."],"a":2,"e":"Neither … nor — verb निकटतम subject (I) के अनुसार 'am'।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Although it was raining but we went out.","Although it was raining, yet we went out.","Although it was raining, so we went out.","Although it was raining, and we went out."],"a":1,"e":"'Although … yet' स्वीकार्य जोड़ी है; although के साथ but/so नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Study hard lest you would fail.","Study hard lest you should not fail.","Study hard lest you may fail.","Study hard lest you should fail."],"a":3,"e":"'Lest … should' — बिना 'not' के।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["He is both rich as well as famous.","He is both rich and famous.","He is both rich and also famous.","He is both rich but famous."],"a":1,"e":"'Both … and' — He is both rich and famous।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["She can neither read or write.","She can neither read nor write.","She can not neither read nor write.","She neither can read nor writes."],"a":1,"e":"'Neither … nor' और दोनों ओर समान रूप (read, write)।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["I would rather walk than to take a bus.","I would rather walk that take a bus.","I would rather to walk than take a bus.","I would rather walk than take a bus."],"a":3,"e":"'Would rather + V1 … than + V1' — दोनों ओर bare infinitive।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["The reason he left is because he was unhappy.","The reason he left is that he was unhappy.","The reason he left is due to he was unhappy.","The reason he left because he was unhappy."],"a":1,"e":"'The reason … is that' — सही संरचना।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Not only he sings but also dances.","Not only does he sing but he also dances.","Not only he does sing but he dances also.","Not only sings he but also dances."],"a":1,"e":"'Not only' आरंभ में → inversion (does he sing), फिर 'but … also'।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Wait till the rain will stop.","Wait till the rain does not stop.","Wait till the rain stops.","Wait till the rain stopped."],"a":2,"e":"'Till' (समय) के साथ future के लिए Simple Present और 'not' नहीं — till the rain stops।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Because he was late so he was punished.","He was punished because he was late.","Because he was late therefore he was punished.","He was punished because of he was late."],"a":1,"e":"Because के साथ so/therefore नहीं; 'because of' के बाद noun आता है, clause नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Either you or he are wrong.","Either you or he is wrong.","Either you or he am wrong.","Either you nor he is wrong."],"a":1,"e":"Either … or — verb निकटतम subject (he) के अनुसार 'is'।"},
    {"q":"Combine using the correct conjunction: 'He is poor. He is honest.'","o":["He is poor and so honest.","He is poor so he is honest.","He is poor because he is honest.","He is poor but honest."],"a":3,"e":"दो विरोधी गुण — 'but' (adversative) से जोड़ते हैं।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He worked hard. He did not pass.'","o":["Though he worked hard, he did not pass.","As he worked hard, he did not pass.","Since he worked hard, he did not pass.","He worked hard so he did not pass."],"a":0,"e":"विरोध (परिश्रम के बावजूद असफल) — 'Though' से जोड़ें।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'Take this medicine. You will get well.'","o":["Take this medicine lest you get well.","Take this medicine or you will get well.","Take this medicine and you will get well.","Take this medicine unless you will get well."],"a":2,"e":"क्रिया और उसका परिणाम — 'and' (Imperative + and = यदि … तो)।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He saw the tiger. He ran away at once.'","o":["He saw the tiger until he ran away.","As soon as he saw the tiger, he ran away.","Unless he saw the tiger, he ran away.","Though he saw the tiger, he ran away."],"a":1,"e":"एक कार्य के तुरंत बाद दूसरा — 'As soon as'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He is very weak. He cannot stand.'","o":["He is too weak to stand.","He is too weak that he cannot stand.","He is so weak to stand.","He is very weak that he cannot stand."],"a":0,"e":"'too … to' = इतना … कि नहीं — He is too weak to stand।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'You must leave now. You will miss the train otherwise.'","o":["You must leave now so that you miss the train.","You must leave now unless you will miss the train.","You must leave now lest you should miss the train.","You must leave now though you miss the train."],"a":2,"e":"'Lest … should' = कहीं ऐसा न हो कि — lest you should miss the train।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'but' in 'He is rich but unhappy'?","o":["Cumulative","Illative","Alternative","Adversative"],"a":3,"e":"'But' विरोध दर्शाता है — Adversative (विरोधसूचक) coordinating conjunction।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'so' in 'It was late, so we went home'?","o":["Illative","Adversative","Alternative","Cumulative"],"a":0,"e":"'So' परिणाम/निष्कर्ष बताता है — Illative conjunction।"},
    {"q":"Which of the following is a correlative conjunction?","o":["because","although","neither … nor","unless"],"a":2,"e":"जोड़ी में आने वाले conjunction correlative कहलाते हैं — neither … nor।"},
    {"q":"Which of the following is a subordinating conjunction?","o":["and","but","or","because"],"a":3,"e":"'Because' आश्रित (कारणवाचक) उपवाक्य जोड़ता है — subordinating; and, but, or coordinating हैं।"},
    {"q":"In 'Since you are tired, you may rest', 'since' expresses:","o":["time","reason","condition","purpose"],"a":1,"e":"यहाँ 'since' = चूँकि (कारण) है, समय नहीं।"},
    {"q":"In 'Poor as he is, he is honest', 'as' means:","o":["though","because","when","like"],"a":0,"e":"'Adjective + as + subject + verb' संरचना में 'as' = though (यद्यपि)।"},
    {"q":"In 'While I was reading, the lights went off', 'while' shows:","o":["contrast","reason","time","condition"],"a":2,"e":"यहाँ 'while' = जब (समय, चल रहे कार्य के दौरान)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: The moment he entered, ______ began to clap.","o":["when everybody","than everybody","then everybody","everybody"],"a":3,"e":"'The moment' स्वयं conjunction (= as soon as) है; इसके साथ when/then/than नहीं जुड़ता।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ had I closed my eyes when the alarm rang.","o":["Barely","No sooner","Not only","As soon"],"a":0,"e":"'Barely/Hardly/Scarcely … when' — No sooner के साथ 'than' आता।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ did I reach home than it began to rain.","o":["Hardly","Scarcely","No sooner","As soon as"],"a":2,"e":"'than' के साथ जोड़ी 'No sooner' की है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He will not come ______ you invite him personally.","o":["so that","unless","lest","until not"],"a":1,"e":"शर्त — यदि तुम व्यक्तिगत रूप से नहीं बुलाओगे तो नहीं आएगा — 'unless'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: You will not succeed ______ you work harder.","o":["if","unless","though","so that"],"a":1,"e":"'Unless' = if not — जब तक अधिक परिश्रम न करो, सफल नहीं होगे।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Ram as well as his brothers ______ coming today.","o":["are","were","have","is"],"a":3,"e":"'As well as' — verb पहले subject (Ram, singular) के अनुसार 'is'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Neither the manager nor the clerks ______ in the office.","o":["were","was","is","has been"],"a":0,"e":"Verb निकटतम subject (clerks, plural) के अनुसार 'were'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Not the students but the principal ______ responsible.","o":["are","were","is","have been"],"a":2,"e":"'Not A but B' — verb B (principal, singular) के अनुसार 'is'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He has no other option ______ to resign.","o":["but that","except that","unless","than"],"a":3,"e":"'Other … than' — no other option than to resign।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He runs ______ a deer.","o":["like","as","as if","as though"],"a":0,"e":"Noun (a deer) से पहले preposition 'like'; clause से पहले 'as'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Fruits ______ mango and guava are rich in vitamins.","o":["such that","such as","so as","as such"],"a":1,"e":"उदाहरण देने हेतु 'such as' (जैसे कि)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is not ______ tall as his brother.","o":["such","more","so","too"],"a":2,"e":"नकारात्मक तुलना में 'not so … as' (या not as … as)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Hurry up, ______ you will be late.","o":["and","if","unless","otherwise"],"a":3,"e":"'Otherwise' = वरना — Hurry up, otherwise you will be late।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I asked him ______ he could help me.","o":["if","that","unless","than"],"a":0,"e":"अप्रत्यक्ष प्रश्न (indirect question) में 'if/whether'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: There is no doubt ______ he is innocent.","o":["whether","if","that","but"],"a":2,"e":"नकारात्मक (no doubt) के बाद 'that' — There is no doubt that…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: It is five years ______ we last met.","o":["for","from","when","since"],"a":3,"e":"'It is + समय + since + Past Simple' — It is five years since we last met।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He did not eat, ______ did he drink anything.","o":["nor","or","and","but"],"a":0,"e":"नकारात्मक वाक्य के बाद 'nor' + inversion (did he)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He saved money ______ he could buy a bicycle.","o":["so that","such that","lest","unless"],"a":0,"e":"उद्देश्य (purpose) बताने के लिए 'so that' — saved money so that he could buy…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: We eat ______ we may live.","o":["unless","in order that","lest","until"],"a":1,"e":"'in order that' भी उद्देश्य बताता है; इसके बाद may/might आता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: You can stay here ______ you keep quiet.","o":["as long as","unless","lest","though"],"a":0,"e":"'as long as' = जब तक / इस शर्त पर कि — शर्त (condition) बताता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Whether you like it ______ not, you must attend the class.","o":["nor","and","than","or"],"a":3,"e":"'whether' का सहसंबंधी (correlative) साथी 'or' है — whether … or not।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Some people like tea, ______ others prefer coffee.","o":["while","because","unless","lest"],"a":0,"e":"दो विपरीत बातों की तुलना (contrast) में 'while/whereas'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Think ______ you speak.","o":["after","until","before","lest"],"a":2,"e":"पहले सोचो, फिर बोलो — समय-क्रम बताने के लिए 'before'।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Put the book back ______ you found it.","o":["when","where","while","which"],"a":1,"e":"स्थान (place) बताने वाला उपवाक्य 'where' से — where you found it।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ he goes, he makes new friends.","o":["Whatever","Whoever","However","Wherever"],"a":3,"e":"'Wherever' = जहाँ कहीं भी (स्थान) — Wherever he goes…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Come to my house ______ you are free.","o":["whenever","whereas","whether","lest"],"a":0,"e":"'whenever' = जब कभी भी (समय)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I will lend you the book on condition ______ you return it soon.","o":["if","that","unless","than"],"a":1,"e":"'on condition that' — शर्त बताने वाला वाक्यांश; 'on condition if' गलत है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ you have come, let us start the meeting.","o":["Unless","Lest","Now that","Until"],"a":2,"e":"'Now that' = चूँकि अब (कारण + वर्तमान स्थिति)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He was ill; ______, he attended the meeting.","o":["nevertheless","therefore","because","unless"],"a":0,"e":"'nevertheless' = फिर भी — विरोध (contrast) बताता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He did not pay the fine; ______ he was sent to jail.","o":["though","lest","unless","hence"],"a":3,"e":"'hence' = इसलिए — परिणाम (illative) बताता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: She is intelligent; ______, she is very hardworking.","o":["moreover","otherwise","unless","whereas"],"a":0,"e":"'moreover' = इसके अतिरिक्त — एक बात में दूसरी बात जोड़ता है (cumulative)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ you learn to swim, you never forget it.","o":["Unless","Lest","Once","Until"],"a":2,"e":"'Once' (conjunction) = एक बार जब — Once you learn…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I will not lend him money ______ he begs me.","o":["even if","so that","as","since"],"a":0,"e":"'even if' = भले ही (काल्पनिक स्थिति में भी) — even if he begs me।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ I know, he is an honest officer.","o":["As long as","As soon as","As far as","As well as"],"a":2,"e":"'As far as I know' = जहाँ तक मुझे पता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: She is no less beautiful ______ her sister.","o":["as","than","then","like"],"a":1,"e":"'no less … than' तुलना का रूप है — no less beautiful than।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He would sooner die ______ surrender.","o":["then","as","but","than"],"a":3,"e":"'sooner … than' (बल्कि … की अपेक्षा) — would sooner die than surrender।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Tell me ______ you solved this sum.","o":["how","which","unless","lest"],"a":0,"e":"Noun clause में तरीका पूछने के लिए 'how' — Tell me how you solved…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: ______ he said was absolutely true.","o":["That","Which","What","Whom"],"a":2,"e":"'What he said' (जो उसने कहा) — noun clause जो subject का काम करता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He said ______ he was very busy.","o":["what","that","which","if"],"a":1,"e":"कथन (reported statement) को जोड़ने के लिए 'that' — He said that…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He is very rich, ______ he lives a simple life.","o":["yet","so","for","or"],"a":0,"e":"'yet' = फिर भी — अपेक्षा के विपरीत बात (adversative)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: After he ______ his work, he went home.","o":["has finished","finishes","had finished","will finish"],"a":2,"e":"भूतकाल में पहले पूरा हुआ कार्य past perfect में — After he had finished…, he went।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: The patient ______ before the doctor came.","o":["dies","has died","had died","would die"],"a":2,"e":"'before' से जुड़े दो भूतकालीन कार्यों में पहले वाला past perfect — had died before the doctor came।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'and' in 'He came and sat down'?","o":["Adversative","Alternative","Illative","Cumulative"],"a":3,"e":"'and' एक कथन में दूसरा जोड़ता है — Cumulative (संयोजक/योजक)।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'or' in 'Work or starve'?","o":["Cumulative","Alternative","Illative","Adversative"],"a":1,"e":"'or' दो विकल्पों में से एक चुनने का भाव देता है — Alternative (विकल्पसूचक)।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'therefore' in 'He was ill; therefore he could not come'?","o":["Adversative","Cumulative","Alternative","Illative"],"a":3,"e":"'therefore' पहले कथन से निष्कर्ष/परिणाम निकालता है — Illative (परिणामसूचक)।"},
    {"q":"Which type of conjunction is 'still' in 'He is old; still he works hard'?","o":["Adversative","Illative","Cumulative","Alternative"],"a":0,"e":"'still' (फिर भी) विरोध/विपरीतता बताता है — Adversative।"},
    {"q":"Which of the following is NOT a coordinating conjunction?","o":["and","but","or","although"],"a":3,"e":"'although' subordinating conjunction है; and, but, or, nor, for, so, yet coordinating हैं।"},
    {"q":"Which of the following is a compound conjunction (a group of words used as a conjunction)?","o":["because","in order that","if","but"],"a":1,"e":"in order that, as soon as, even if, so that, as though — शब्द-समूह जो conjunction का काम करें, compound conjunctions हैं।"},
    {"q":"The conjunction 'lest' expresses:","o":["Positive purpose","Condition","Negative purpose","Time"],"a":2,"e":"'lest' = ऐसा न हो कि — negative purpose (नकारात्मक उद्देश्य); इसके बाद 'should' आता है।"},
    {"q":"The conjunction 'unless' introduces a clause of:","o":["Condition","Time","Place","Comparison"],"a":0,"e":"'unless' = यदि … नहीं — Condition (शर्त) का उपवाक्य।"},
    {"q":"In 'I know that he is honest', the clause 'that he is honest' is a/an:","o":["Adverb clause","Adjective clause","Noun clause","Principal clause"],"a":2,"e":"यह उपवाक्य verb 'know' का object है — Noun clause।"},
    {"q":"In 'He sat where his father had sat', the clause 'where his father had sat' is an adverb clause of:","o":["Time","Place","Reason","Manner"],"a":1,"e":"'where' स्थान बताता है — Adverb clause of Place।"},
    {"q":"Which pair is a correct correlative conjunction?","o":["Neither … or","Both … as well as","Whether … or","Not only … and"],"a":2,"e":"सही युग्म: whether … or, either … or, neither … nor, both … and, not only … but also।"},
    {"q":"In 'He worked hard so that he might succeed', 'so that' expresses:","o":["Result","Reason","Condition","Purpose"],"a":3,"e":"'so that' उद्देश्य (purpose) बताता है; 'so … that' (He is so weak that…) परिणाम बताता है।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: She asked me (A) / that whether I (B) / could help her. (C) / No error (D)","o":["She asked me","that whether I","could help her","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'that' और 'whether' दोनों एक साथ नहीं आते — 'She asked me whether I could help her'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He worked hard (A) / so that he may (B) / pass the exam. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He worked hard","so that he may","pass the exam","No error"],"a":1,"e":"मुख्य वाक्य past tense (worked) में हो तो 'so that' के बाद 'might/could' — so that he might pass।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Both the boy and the girl (A) / was punished (B) / for coming late. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Both the boy and the girl","was punished","for coming late","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'Both … and' से जुड़ा subject बहुवचन होता है — 'were punished'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He is as good (A) / if not better than (B) / his brother. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He is as good","if not better than","his brother","No error"],"a":0,"e":"दोनों तुलनाएँ पूरी होनी चाहिए — 'He is as good as, if not better than, his brother'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: I have never seen (A) / such a beautiful palace (B) / like this. (C) / No error (D)","o":["I have never seen","such a beautiful palace","like this","No error"],"a":2,"e":"'such' के बाद 'as' आता है — 'such a beautiful palace as this'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Supposing if (A) / he does not come, (B) / what will you do? (C) / No error (D)","o":["Supposing if","he does not come,","what will you do?","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'Supposing' स्वयं शर्त का भाव देता है, 'if' अनावश्यक — 'Supposing he does not come…'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Until and unless (A) / you work hard, (B) / you cannot succeed. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Until and unless","you work hard,","you cannot succeed","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'Until and unless' दोहराव है — केवल 'Unless you work hard…'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: In spite he was ill, (A) / he came to the office (B) / on time. (C) / No error (D)","o":["In spite he was ill,","he came to the office","on time","No error"],"a":0,"e":"'in spite of' preposition है, उपवाक्य नहीं जोड़ता — 'Though he was ill' या 'In spite of being ill'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He was such (A) / tired that (B) / he fell asleep at once. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He was such","tired that","he fell asleep at once","No error"],"a":0,"e":"अकेले adjective (tired) के साथ 'so … that'; 'such' के बाद noun आता है — 'He was so tired that…'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: As soon as he arrived, (A) / then (B) / the meeting began. (C) / No error (D)","o":["As soon as he arrived,","then","the meeting began","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'As soon as' के साथ 'then' अनावश्यक — 'As soon as he arrived, the meeting began'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Although he worked hard, (A) / he could not (B) / get through the exam. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Although he worked hard,","he could not","get through the exam","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'Although' के साथ 'but' नहीं आया है और वाक्य पूर्ण है — कोई त्रुटि नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: I do not know (A) / if or not (B) / he will come. (C) / No error (D)","o":["I do not know","if or not","he will come","No error"],"a":1,"e":"'or not' के साथ 'whether' आता है — 'whether or not he will come'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He was not only (A) / a great poet (B) / but also a great painter. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He was not only","a great poet","but also a great painter","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'not only' और 'but also' दोनों के बाद समान रचना (a great poet / a great painter) — वाक्य शुद्ध है।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'She was tired. She kept working.'","o":["She was tired, so she kept working.","She was tired because she kept working.","She was tired unless she kept working.","She was tired; nevertheless, she kept working."],"a":3,"e":"दोनों वाक्यों में विरोध है — 'nevertheless' (फिर भी) से जोड़ना उचित।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'You must work hard. Then you will pass.'","o":["If you work hard, you will pass.","Unless you work hard, you will pass.","Lest you work hard, you will pass.","Though you work hard, you will pass."],"a":0,"e":"शर्त और उसका परिणाम — 'If you work hard, you will pass'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'Ram is clever. Shyam is also clever.'","o":["Either Ram or Shyam is clever.","Both Ram and Shyam are clever.","Neither Ram nor Shyam is clever.","Ram is clever but Shyam is clever."],"a":1,"e":"दोनों में समान गुण — 'Both … and' + plural verb 'are'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He did not come. He did not phone.'","o":["He neither came nor phoned.","He either came or phoned.","He came but did not phone.","He did not come but phoned."],"a":0,"e":"दो नकारात्मक कथन — 'neither … nor' से जोड़ते हैं।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'She sings. She also dances.'","o":["She sings unless she dances.","She sings lest she dances.","She not only sings but also dances.","She neither sings nor dances."],"a":2,"e":"एक बात के साथ दूसरी बात पर बल — 'not only … but also'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He stood on a chair. He wanted to see the procession clearly.'","o":["He stood on a chair lest he could see clearly.","He stood on a chair unless he could see clearly.","He stood on a chair though he could see clearly.","He stood on a chair so that he could see the procession clearly."],"a":3,"e":"दूसरा वाक्य उद्देश्य बताता है — 'so that he could see…'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He was ill. He did not attend the class.'","o":["As he was ill, he did not attend the class.","Though he was ill, he did not attend the class.","Unless he was ill, he did not attend the class.","As he was ill, so he did not attend the class."],"a":0,"e":"कारण बताने के लिए 'As' — इसके साथ 'so' नहीं लगाया जाता।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'The sun set. The farmers returned home.'","o":["The sun set unless the farmers returned home.","When the sun set, the farmers returned home.","The sun set lest the farmers returned home.","Though the sun set, the farmers returned home."],"a":1,"e":"समय का संबंध — 'When the sun set, …'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'Walk carefully. You may slip otherwise.'","o":["Walk carefully so that you may slip.","Walk carefully unless you slip.","Walk carefully lest you should slip.","Walk carefully until you slip."],"a":2,"e":"नकारात्मक उद्देश्य (ऐसा न हो कि) — 'lest you should slip'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He is very honest. Everyone trusts him.'","o":["He is too honest that everyone trusts him.","He is such honest that everyone trusts him.","He is honest lest everyone trusts him.","He is so honest that everyone trusts him."],"a":3,"e":"कारण और परिणाम — 'so + adjective + that'।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'I do not know the answer. My friend does not know it either.'","o":["Neither I nor my friend knows the answer.","Either I or my friend know the answer.","Neither I nor my friend know the answer.","Both I and my friend knows the answer."],"a":0,"e":"'Neither … nor' में verb निकटतम subject (my friend — singular) के अनुसार — knows।"},
    {"q":"Combine: 'He is poor. He is contented.'","o":["He is poor and so contented.","He is poor, yet he is contented.","He is poor, so he is contented.","He is poor because he is contented."],"a":1,"e":"अपेक्षा के विपरीत बात — 'yet' (adversative)।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Because his illness, he could not come.","Because of he was ill, he could not come.","Due to he was ill, he could not come.","Because of his illness, he could not come."],"a":3,"e":"noun/phrase (his illness) से पहले 'because of' (preposition); उपवाक्य (he was ill) से पहले 'because' (conjunction)।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["I do not know whether or not he will agree.","I do not know if or not he will agree.","I do not know that whether he will agree.","I do not know whether he will agree or no."],"a":0,"e":"'whether or not' सही; 'if or not' और 'that whether' गलत; 'or no' के स्थान पर 'or not'।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Since he is rich, so he is proud.","He is proud as he is rich.","As he is rich, therefore he is proud.","Because he is rich, hence he is proud."],"a":1,"e":"कारण वाले conjunction (as, since, because) के साथ so/therefore/hence नहीं लगते।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Hardly he had left than she arrived.","Hardly had he left than she arrived.","No sooner had he left than she arrived.","No sooner he left when she arrived."],"a":2,"e":"'No sooner had … than' — inversion और 'than' दोनों आवश्यक।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["He works hard so that he may succeed.","He works hard so that he might succeeds.","He works hard so that he may not fail lest.","He works hard lest he may succeed."],"a":0,"e":"वर्तमान काल के मुख्य वाक्य के साथ 'so that … may'।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Wherever you go, I shall follow you.","Whenever you go, I shall follow you there wherever.","Where you will go, there I shall follow you wherever.","Wherever you will go, I shall follow you."],"a":0,"e":"'Wherever' वाले उपवाक्य में भविष्य के लिए भी present tense — Wherever you go।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["She is so kind lady that all respect her.","She is such kind lady that all respect her.","She is such a kind lady that all respect her.","She is so a kind lady that all respect her."],"a":2,"e":"'such + a/an + adjective + noun + that' — such a kind lady that…।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["While walking in the garden, a snake bit him.","While he was walking in the garden, a snake bit him.","While he walking in the garden, a snake bit him.","While was he walking in the garden, a snake bit him."],"a":1,"e":"'While walking…' का कर्ता 'a snake' बन जाता है (dangling); उपवाक्य में अपना subject और पूर्ण verb चाहिए — While he was walking…।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["For he was ill, he could not come.","He could not come, for he was ill.","He could not come, for that he was ill.","He could not come for because he was ill."],"a":1,"e":"Coordinating 'for' (क्योंकि) वाला उपवाक्य मुख्य वाक्य के बाद आता है, वाक्य के आरंभ में नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Unless it rains, the match will be held.","Unless it does not rain, the match will be held.","Unless it will rain, the match will be held.","Unless it rains not, the match will be held."],"a":0,"e":"'unless' में स्वयं 'नहीं' का भाव है; इसके साथ 'not' या 'will' नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["She asked me that whether I was free.","She asked me whether I was free.","She asked me that if I was free.","She asked to me whether I was free."],"a":1,"e":"प्रश्नवाचक कथन को 'whether/if' जोड़ता है, 'that' के साथ नहीं; 'asked me' (to नहीं)।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["I have been waiting since two hours.","Ever since he left, the house has been quiet.","Ever since he has left, the house was quiet.","Ever since he left, the house was being quiet."],"a":1,"e":"'since' वाला उपवाक्य past tense में, मुख्य वाक्य present perfect में — Ever since he left, the house has been quiet।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["Hurry up unless you will miss the bus.","Hurry up lest you will miss the bus.","Hurry up or else you will miss the bus.","Hurry up and else you will miss the bus."],"a":2,"e":"'or else' (वरना) चेतावनी/विकल्प बताता है — Hurry up or else you will miss the bus।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Search ______ you will find.","o":["unless","lest","though","and"],"a":3,"e":"आदेश + परिणाम को 'and' जोड़ता है — Search and you will find (खोजो तो पाओगे)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: Is the statement true ______ false?","o":["nor","but","or","than"],"a":2,"e":"दो विकल्पों में से एक पूछने के लिए 'or' (alternative)।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He was fined ______ he broke the traffic rules.","o":["lest","unless","though","because"],"a":3,"e":"कारण बताने के लिए 'because' — fined because he broke…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: I do not know ______ he is angry with me.","o":["whom","lest","why","unless"],"a":2,"e":"कारण पूछने वाला noun clause 'why' से — I do not know why…।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: No one knows ______ he has gone.","o":["whom","where","lest","unless"],"a":1,"e":"स्थान के बारे में अप्रत्यक्ष प्रश्न — No one knows where he has gone।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: This is the reason ______ I came late.","o":["because","lest","unless","why"],"a":3,"e":"'the reason why …' — reason के बाद 'because' नहीं, 'why/that' आता है।"},
    {"q":"Fill in the blank: He reached the station ______ the train had left.","o":["after","before","unless","lest"],"a":0,"e":"पहले ट्रेन गई (had left), फिर वह पहुँचा — 'after the train had left'।"},
    {"q":"In 'Do as I say', the conjunction 'as' denotes:","o":["Reason","Time","Manner","Comparison"],"a":2,"e":"'as' = जैसे — कार्य करने का ढंग (manner) बताता है।"},
    {"q":"In 'He is taller than I am', 'than' introduces a clause of:","o":["Comparison","Condition","Purpose","Concession"],"a":0,"e":"'than' तुलना (comparison) का उपवाक्य जोड़ता है।"},
    {"q":"In 'If you come, I will go', the clause 'If you come' is a/an:","o":["Noun clause","Adjective clause","Principal clause","Adverb clause of condition"],"a":3,"e":"'if' शर्त बताता है और क्रिया की परिस्थिति बताता है — Adverb clause of Condition।"},
    {"q":"In 'The man who came here is my uncle', the clause 'who came here' is a/an:","o":["Adverb clause","Noun clause","Adjective clause","Principal clause"],"a":2,"e":"यह उपवाक्य noun 'man' की विशेषता बताता है — Adjective (relative) clause।"},
    {"q":"Which of the following conjunctions shows concession (contrast)?","o":["because","though","if","so that"],"a":1,"e":"'though/although/even though' = यद्यपि — concession (विरोध के बावजूद)।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: She is so beautiful (A) / as (B) / her elder sister. (C) / No error (D)","o":["She is so beautiful","as","her elder sister","No error"],"a":0,"e":"सकारात्मक वाक्य में बराबरी की तुलना 'as … as' से — 'She is as beautiful as…'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: I am sure (A) / whether he (B) / will come. (C) / No error (D)","o":["I am sure","whether he","will come","No error"],"a":1,"e":"निश्चितता (sure) के बाद 'that' — 'I am sure that he will come'; संदेह में whether।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He asked me (A) / why was I (B) / late. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He asked me","why was I","late","No error"],"a":1,"e":"अप्रत्यक्ष प्रश्न (noun clause) में कथन जैसा क्रम — 'why I was late'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: When I reached (A) / the station, (B) / the train already left. (C) / No error (D)","o":["When I reached","the station,","the train already left","No error"],"a":2,"e":"पहले घटी घटना के लिए past perfect — 'the train had already left'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He was so tired (A) / that he cannot (B) / walk any further. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He was so tired","that he cannot","walk any further","No error"],"a":1,"e":"मुख्य वाक्य past (was) में हो तो 'that' उपवाक्य भी past में — 'that he could not'।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Before I could (A) / reach the hospital, (B) / my uncle had died. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Before I could","reach the hospital,","my uncle had died","No error"],"a":3,"e":"पहले घटित घटना (had died) past perfect में और 'before' के साथ — वाक्य शुद्ध है।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Since (A) / it was raining heavily, (B) / we stayed at home. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Since","it was raining heavily,","we stayed at home","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'Since' कारण के अर्थ में सही प्रयोग, साथ में 'so' नहीं — कोई त्रुटि नहीं।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: He walked (A) / so fast that (B) / I could not keep pace with him. (C) / No error (D)","o":["He walked","so fast that","I could not keep pace with him","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'so + adverb + that' और दोनों भाग past tense में — वाक्य शुद्ध है।"},
    {"q":"Spot the error: Ravi is hardworking (A) / whereas (B) / his brother is lazy. (C) / No error (D)","o":["Ravi is hardworking","whereas","his brother is lazy","No error"],"a":3,"e":"'whereas' दो विपरीत तथ्यों की तुलना करता है — वाक्य शुद्ध है।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["She preferred to walk than take the bus.","She preferred to walk rather than take the bus.","She preferred walking than taking the bus.","She preferred to walk rather to take the bus."],"a":1,"e":"'prefer' के साथ infinitive हो तो 'rather than' — preferred to walk rather than take…।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["She asked me where did I live.","She asked me where do I live.","She asked me where I lived.","She asked me that where I lived."],"a":2,"e":"अप्रत्यक्ष प्रश्न में कथन-क्रम (subject + verb) और past tense — where I lived।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["He is as strong as, if not stronger than, his brother.","He is as strong, if not stronger than, his brother.","He is strong as, if not stronger than, his brother.","He is as strong if not stronger as his brother."],"a":0,"e":"दोनों तुलनाएँ पूरी — 'as strong as, if not stronger than'।"},
    {"q":"Choose the correct sentence.","o":["He both lost his money and his friends.","Both he lost his money and his friends.","He lost both his money and his friends.","He lost both his money as well as his friends."],"a":2,"e":"'both … and' ठीक उन समान शब्दों (his money / his friends) से पहले आते हैं; 'both … as well as' गलत।"}
  ]
});
